********************  PMoria 0.98 Modifications  ****************************

Commands/Inventory:

  Can (W)ield arrows/iron shots to put them in quiver.  Then press 's' to
(s)hoot the arrow in a direction.  Note:  Must use the # (Searching Mode)
command to search.

New Items:

 Barbed Arrows (2d8)    --- expensive and heavy
 Ice Sword (Dwarven)    --- automatic (FB)
 Flame Sword (Dwarven)  --- automatic (FT)
 Slicer Sword (Avion) (3d5)
 Iron-Shod Boots

New Ego Attributes:

 (DB)  -  (SA) (SE) (SD) (SU) BUT -(3-5) to Stealth.  Very rare.
 (EL)  -  (FT) (FB) (RC) (RF) See Invis.
 (TD)  -  + to Stealth, See Invis, Free Act, Regen

Prayer List Changes:

  Added Divine Orb (more powerful Orb of Draining), and changed Holy Word so
it does more.

  Added Return Home (Word of Recall) at low level

Mage List Changes:

  Added Acid Ball
  
  Added Magic Warp (Word of Recall) at high level

  Changed Recharge II to Solar Ball (Lightning ball), made Recharge I grow in
power as you grow in level

  Increased spell damage, since ALL spells decrease over distance cast (for
Mage/Priest/Sage)

Sage magic class added (find out spells and effects for yourself)

New Races:

 Avion (half-bird)  --- strong, fast, excellent (80 ft) infravision, fair
stealth, fair dex

 Spectre (replaces Gnome) --- Very weak, few HP, but has incredible innate
AC and resistance to physical attacks

 Sage Elf --- Very wise Elf, makes GREAT Priests

New Classes:

 Healer --- gets healing Priestly prayers quickly, has many HP, good stealth,
but can cast NO other spells

 Sage --- totally new magic class.  Fair fighter, good with Bows and Magic
Devices, few HP

 Jester --- very well-balanced character class.  No strengths, no weaknesses.
Fair magic.

 Demigod --- very powerful, great fighter, lots of HP, gets all low-level
Priestly prayers, cannot Disarm or use Bows well at all, miserable Stealth.

 Monk --- uses NO weapons OR armor, but has high innate AC (starts at 50, and
goes up by 2 per level).  Has decent HP, but hits VERY rarely.  When does hit,
tends to kill opponent (50 points of damage is common for 1st level)

NOTE:  Any character can wear boots and/or a cloak.  Armor refers to headgear,
gloves, and body armor.

Class Changes:

 Warriors have innate (RF) (RC) and (RG) (Resist Poison Gas), get more blows/
round with heavy weapons, get automatic +to-hit and +to-dam bonuses which
increase with level.  Have excellent resistance to XP drain.

 Rogues are resistant to pickpocket attacks, get more blows/round with light
weapons, get automatic AC bonus if wearing light armor.  Good resistance to
XP drain.

 All classes have an upper limit on how heavy armor they can wear (and some
classes---Healers and Monks---cannot wear ANY armor)

  

